# Repo-internal files — kept in the repo but not served on the public site.
#
# Cloudflare Pages deploys every committed file, which was publishing the
# migration guide (naming the Cloudflare account, Supabase project ref and
# deploy tokens), the PowerShell scripts, and the raw brand kit. None of it
# is needed by the site; MIGRATION.md still has to live in the repo so the
# next machine move works from a clean clone.
#
# Format: <path> <destination> <status>.  404 serves the destination with a
# 404 status, so these paths read as "not found" to the public.

/MIGRATION.md                   /   404
/README.md                      /   404
/serve.ps1                      /   404
/deploy.ps1                     /   404
/deploy-github.ps1              /   404
/deploy-netlify-redirect.ps1    /   404

# Source brand kit: unreferenced by the site (fonts load from assets/fonts/),
# and contains licensed font files plus __MACOSX junk.
/brand-assets/*                 /   404
